# R5-2 (steps/array-receiver-20261011.md, "R5-2, design before code"): the author's staged bindings -- a name bound to
# the Array a value selects is a descriptor reference cell carrying that Array's contract: `[]: []: b a` holds the
# two-level a, `[]: c: a[1]` and `[]: d a[1]` hold the row stored in a's cell, `[]: e: b[1]` a level selected through a
# binding, `[]: []: f b` a binding's Array again; `length` reads the held Array, and an element write through a binding
# is seen through the row -- one Array, two references.  Before: "unsupported own array declaration".  Natively and
# with the methods walked.  Entry 7.
fn: work () int
    []: []: int a 2
    []: int row 3
    a[1]: row
    []: []: b a
    []: c: a[1]
    []: d a[1]
    if: length(b) != 2U || length(c) != 3U || length(d) != 3U || length(b[1]) != 3U
        return: 81
    c[0]: 9
    d[2]: 4
    if: row[0] != 9 || row[2] != 4 || c[2] != 4
        return: 82
    []: e: b[1]
    []: []: f b
    if: length(e) != 3U || length(f) != 2U
        return: 83
    e[1]: 5
    if: row[1] != 5 || d[1] != 5
        return: 84
    return: 7
end: work
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: work(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
